          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em Kac-Moody Lie algebra
            is a generalization of that of
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semisimple+Lie+algebra"} semisimple Lie algebra
            to infinite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of the underlying
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#kacmoody_algebras Kac-Moody algebras
          %p
            Recall that the Lie algebra of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sl%282%29"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔩
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sl}_2
            admits a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi h
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h,e,f)
            on which the non-vanishing
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+brackets"} Lie brackets
            are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mi h
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtext and
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "right center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi h
                        %mo ,
                        %mi e
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi e
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mi h
                        %mo ,
                        %mi f
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mtd
                        %mo =
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 2
                        %mi f
                        %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                          %mrow
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [e,f] \;=\; h
                  \\;\;\;\text{and}\;\;\;
                  \\begin{array}{rcl}
                  [h,e] &amp;=&amp; \phantom{-}2 e
                  \\\
                  [h,f] &amp;=&amp; -2 f
                  \\mathrlap{\,.}
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            A Kac-Moody Lie algebra is generated from a set of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{N}
            such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔰𝔩
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sl}_2
            generators,
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h_i, e_i, f_i)_{i = 1}^r
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+Cartan+matrix"} generalized Cartan matrix
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi A
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mi j
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A = (A_{i j})_{i,j=1}^r
          #eq:GeneralizedCartanMatrix.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "center left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo ∈
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mi ℤ
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mi i
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ≠
                            %mi j
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                      %mtd
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⇔
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %munder
                          %mo ∃
                          %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi D
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi DiagMat
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi r
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi r
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mrow
                                %mi S
                                %mo ∈
                                %msub
                                  %mi SymMat
                                  %mrow
                                    %mi r
                                    %mo ×
                                    %mi r
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi ℤ
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtd
                        %mi A
                        %mo =
                        %mi D
                        %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{cl}
                  \\underset{i,j}{\forall} &amp;
                  A_{i j} \,\in\, \mathbb{Z}
                  \\\
                  \\underset{i}{\forall} &amp;
                  A_{i i} = 2
                  \\\
                  \\underset{i \neq j}{\forall} &amp;
                  A_{i j} \leq 0
                  \\\
                  \\underset{i, j}{\forall} &amp;
                  A_{i j} = 0 \;\Leftrightarrow\; A_{j i} = 0
                  \\\
                  \\underset{
                  { D \in DiagMat_{r \times r}(\mathbb{Z}) }
                  \\atop
                  { S \in SymMat_{r \times r}(\mathbb{Z}) }
                  }{\exists} &amp;
                  A = D S
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            (where in the last line
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/diagonal+matrix"} diagonal matrix
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+matrix"} symmetric matrix
          %p
            via the following
            = succeed ":" do
              %em Chevalley relations
          #eq:ChevalleyRelations.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (2)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mphantom
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo −
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi j
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %msub
                          %mi h
                          %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{l}
                  [h_i, h_j] \,=\, 0
                  \\\
                  [h_i, e_j] \,=\, \phantom{-}A_{i j} e_j
                  \\\
                  [h_i, f_j] \,=\, -A_{i j} f_j
                  \\\
                  [e_i, f_i] \,=\, \delta_{i j} h_j
                  \\end{array}
          %p
            and subject to the following
            %em Serre relations
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+action"} adjoint action
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ad
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ∶−
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ad(e_i)(-) \,\coloneq\,[e_i,-]
          #eq:SerreRelations.maruku-equation
            %span.maruku-eq-number (3)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mtable{:columnalign => "left", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi ad
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                    %mtr
                      %mtd
                        %mi ad
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi f
                          %mi i
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mn 1
                            %mo −
                            %msub
                              %mi A
                              %mi ij
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi e
                          %mi j
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo =
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mn 0
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{array}{l}
                  ad(e_i)^{1 - A_{ij}}(e_j) \,=\, 0
                  \\\
                  ad(f_i)^{1 - A_{ij}}(e_j) \,=\, 0
                  \\,.
                  \\end{array}
          %p
          #KacMoodyAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A
              %em Kac-Moody algebra
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+Lie+algebra"} rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \,\in\,\mathbb{N}
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphic
              to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+Lie+algebra"} free Lie algebra
              on generators
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi e
                      %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %msubsup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (h_i, e_i, f_i)_{i=1}^r
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+ideal"} Lie ideal
              generated by the Chevalley relations
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:ChevalleyRelations"} (2)
              and the Serre relations
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:SerreRelations"} (3)
              for some generalized Cartan matrix
              = succeed "." do
                %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:GeneralizedCartanMatrix"} (1)
          %p
            The generalized Cartan matrix
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_A
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %em simply-laced
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %munder
                        %mo ∀
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo ≠
                          %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %msub
                        %mi A
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mi j
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo ∈
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i \neq j}{\forall}\; A_{i j} \,\in\, \{0,-1\}
            %li
              %p
                %em symmetric
                if
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mo ∀
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi j
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \underset{i, j}{\forall}\; A_{i j} = A_{j i}
          %p
            A symmetric generalized Cartan matrix is equivalently encoded in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dynkin+diagram"} Dynkin diagram
            that it is the coincidence matrix of: The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/undirected+graph"} undirected graph
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vertices"} vertices
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi A
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_{i j}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edges"} edges
            between the
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi j
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j
          %h3#OnMaximalCompactSubalgebra Maximal-compact (involutory) subalgebras
          %p
          #CartanChevalleyInvolution.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              Given a Kac-Moody algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{g}_A
              (according to Def.
              = succeed ")," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KacMoodyAlgebra"}
              %em Cartan-Chevalley involution
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra"} Lie algebra
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              given on generators by
            #eq:CartanChevalleyInvolutionOnGenerators.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (4)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "center center center", :displaystyle => "false", :rowspacing => "0.5ex"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi θ
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi 𝔤
                            %mi A
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi f
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi e
                            %mi i
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mi i
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↦
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %msub
                            %mi h
                            %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{array}{ccc}
                    \\mathfrak{g}_A
                    \&amp;\xrightarrow{\;\; \theta \;\;}&amp;
                    \\mathfrak{g}_A
                    \\\
                    e_i &amp;\mapsto&amp; - f_i
                    \\\
                    f_i &amp;\mapsto&amp; - e_i
                    \\\
                    h_i &amp;\mapsto&amp; - h_i
                    \\end{array}
            %p
          It is clear that
          %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:CartanChevalleyInvolutionOnGenerators"} (4)
          is an
          = succeed ":" do
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/involution"} involution
          = succeed "." do
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi θ
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi θ
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} id
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \theta \circ \theta \,=\, \mathrm{id}
          %p
          #MaximalCompactSubalgebra.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %em maximal compact
              (or
              = succeed ")" do
                %em involutory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔨
                      %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{k}_A \,\subset\, \mathfrak{g}_A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+locus"} fixed locus
              of the Cartan-Chevalley involution (Def.
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CartanChevalleyInvolution"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔨
                      %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi 𝔨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≔
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ∈
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔤
                      %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} }
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathfrak{k}_A
                    \\,\coloneqq\,
                    \\mathfrak{k}(\mathfrak{g}_A)
                    \\;\coloneqq\;
                    \\big\{
                    x \,\in\, \mathfrak{g}_A
                    \\,\big\vert\,
                    \\theta(x) = x
                    \\big\}
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            For Kac-Moody algebras which are Lie algebras of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+Lie+groups"} classical Lie groups
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#MaximalCompactSubalgebra"}
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/maximal+compact+subgroup"} maximal compact subgroup
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The Cartan-Chevalley involution on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sl%28n%29"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔰𝔩
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{sl}_n
              is, in its canonical
              = succeed "-incarnation," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix+Lie+algebra"} matrix Lie algebra
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transpose+matrices"} transpose matrices
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi θ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %msup
                      %mi x
                      %mi T
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\theta(x) \;=\; -x^T
                    \\,,
            %p
              whence the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fixed+locus"} fixed locus
              is
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/so%28n%29"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi 𝔰𝔬
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{so}_n
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔨
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔩
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:maxsize => "1.2em", :minsize => "1.2em"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔰𝔬
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathfrak{k}\big(
                    \\mathfrak{sl}_n(\mathbb{R})
                    \\big)
                    \\;\simeq\;
                    \\mathfrak{so}_n(\mathbb{R})
                    \\,.
            %p
          %p
            Generalizing from this, it may often be useful to think of the involutory subalgebra as consisting of the anti-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hermitian+matrix"} Hermitian
            elements.
          %p
            %br/
          %h2#examples Examples
          %p
            The sequence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exceptional+Lie+group"} exceptional semisimple Lie algebras
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E6"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝔢
                        %mn 6
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{e}_6
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E7"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝔢
                      %mn 7
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{e}_7
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/E8"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
